I'll also comment that "suffer" is a pretty strong
term for a trivial inconvenience. My grandfather,
in his later years, had cataracts so dense he could
only read using paired eight power magnifying
glasses in the form of jewelers' loupes on his
eyeglasses, yet I never once heard him describe what
he was doing as "suffering", nor did it diminish his
love of reading a good book after dinner.

Life contains inconveniences. It is an inconvenience
that I've been whiplashed in five auto accidents,
and that my spine screams as I sit here posting, but
I'm not "suffering", I'm just leading a normal human
existence with the same sorts of undesirable nerve
messages everyone else my age receives.

Usenet should be renamed: Land of the Whingers, if
